      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has significant understandability issues:\n1. Dozens of unused imports\n2. Many unused data-provider methods (only `data_samples` is referenced by a `@MethodSource`)\n3. The `data_samples()` array is all on one long line, making it nearly impossible to read\n\nLet me write the improved version.Now let me compile-check the file.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored file removes all unused imports and dead data-provider methods, and reformats `data_samples()` with one entry per line and inline comments that explain the Discordian/ISO year relationship, the St. Tib's Day leap-day row, and the historical boundary cases — making the test's intent immediately clear to any reader."
